Z||000002||batboy||06-29-2000||10:51 AM||||Careful kid, you'll shoot your eye out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||06-29-2000||01:14 PM||||At the car shows when enduraflex first came out one of the demonstractions was to take a bowling ball attached to a chain ala wrecking ball, and to swing it as hard as you could at an unpainted door panel. (of course the paint can't take that kind of punishment) but the door certainly could. That exhibit is now in the possesion of the Fiero Owners Club of a America.||||reg||2
Z||000004||1FST2M6||06-29-2000||01:19 PM||||odds are the panel was cold when it got hit by said bat. I drove over a door panel and it made LOTS of strange noises but didn't crack... ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Boodoggin||06-29-2000||04:24 PM||||In chemistry one day we were lerning about the importance of petroleum based plastics. It was an old movie and they said new cars were coming out with space age technology plastics.  Then they showed the fiero manufacturing plant!  Then the host of the program started kicking the crap out of a fiero door to show how strong it was.  He said something like "these are the cars of the future"||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||06-29-2000||05:22 PM||||I remember when I was maybe 11 or 12 my dad and I test drove a black 87 coupe. My neighbors and myself thought it was the coolest car around. My mom took lots of pictures, one of which I have on my refrigerator. Back at the dealership, the salesman demonstrated how strong the panels are by in the showroom by striking a door with a hammer they had for display. Lots of kids had fun with that!!<BR>Shortly after a neighbor bought a different black 87 coupe with a gold Pegasus emblem on the hood, and another neighbor bought a loaded red 88GT, which he currently owns, with 12,000 miles on it. I saw it last week when I was in MD. <BR>See what we started!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
